  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Switch places and go for goal",
  "description": "Two attackers against two defenders and a goalkeeper in one half of the rink. Two support players stand at the centre line with the balls. They play the ball in and take passes back, but never skate into the play themselves.\n\nThe attackers keep moving and switch places – for example by crossing – to lose their defender and get free on goal. Offside applies, so no attacker may be past the defenders when the support player plays the ball. The defenders start at half pace. A try ends with a goal, a save, a won ball or the ball going out. Rotate in pairs after a few tries: attackers become support, support become defenders and defenders become attackers.\n\nVariant: fully active defenders, and the pairs compete. A goal scores for both the attackers and the support players. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Switch at speed – one run pulls a defender along and opens the ice for the other."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Time your run so you are onside when the ball is played: wait for the pass, then go past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Use the support: play it back rather than lose the ball in the crowd in front of goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Support: play the ball ahead of the skater so they can take it at full speed."
    }
  ],
